[00:08.18] This big highway goes from coast to coast,
[00:12.30] From New Yorker town down to Los Angeles;
[00:16.94] It's named for Willy Rogers that went on this road
[00:21.54] From New Yorker town down to Los Angeles .
[00:27.96] My Sixty-Six highway, this Will Rogers road,
[00:32.62] It's lined with jalopies just as far as I can see;
[00:41.20] Can you think up a joke, Will, for all o'these folks
[00:42.26] From New Yorker town down to Lost Angeles?
[00:52.14] Ten thousand lost families I count every day
[00:56.02] Caught under my bridges and under my trees;
[01:01.14] Can you make up a joke that'll win them a job
[01:05.76] From New Yorker town down to Lost Angeles?
[01:13.40] I love Willy Rogers, I love your big smile,
[01:19.46] I go to my showhouse, Will Rogers to see;
[01:24.10] Can you grin up a tale that'll feed my folks stranded
[01:28.42] 'Twist New Yorker town and Lost Angeles?
[01:33.56] This Will Rogers highroad I hitched lots o'times;
[01:38.58] All day long you sizzle; all night long I freeze;
[01:43.10] Did ye tickle Hoover enuf ta build us all houses
[01:44.82] From New Yorker town down to Lost Angeles?
[01:57.20] Willy Rogers got born down around Oolagah,
[02:00.48] In my great Indian nation of the Cherokee;
[02:05.12] My Indians all call this the Hungry Gut Highway
[02:09.38] From New Yorker town down to Lost Angeles.
[02:21.60] I bummed this good road with folks you call Goons,
[02:24.24] And your high families called us the lost refugees;
[02:51.74] You hafta go back, Will, and tickle 'em again
[02:58.14] From New Yorker town down to Lost Angeles.
